      "content": "What are the symptoms of dengue?",
      "id": "319e2fb8-74f0-45a1-9301-8399d973f4b0",
      "created_at": "2026-06-28T18:39:34.665391"
    },
    {
      "conversation_id": "b6f5f163-b714-4935-89ea-1ac25260b954",
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The symptoms of dengue include:\n\n1. **High Blood Sugar Levels**: The most common symptom is high blood sugar levels, which can cause severe dehydration and electrolyte imbalances.\n2. **Fatigue and Weakness**: People often feel very tired and weak, especially if they have been infected multiple times.\n3. **Severe Headaches**: Dizziness, headaches, and confusion are also common.\n4. **Muscle Pain**: Many patients experience muscle pain, particularly in the legs and arms.\n5. **Vomiting**: Some people may experience vomiting, which can be severe.\n6. **Diarrhea**: Diarrhea is another common symptom, especially in children.\n7. **Chills and Fever**: In some cases, patients may develop chills and fever.\n8. **Loss of Appetite**: Loss of appetite is common and can lead to malnutrition.\n9. **Abdominal Cramps**: Abdominal cramps can occur due to fluid loss.\n10. **Fatigue**: Despite feeling well, patients may still feel extremely fatigued.\n\nThese symptoms can be severe and require prompt medical attention. It's important to seek medical help immediately if any of these symptoms appear.",
